1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,280
So, we're kind of out of a series in a series.

2
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:19,860
We have put together a series to walk through our vision and our mission and our core practices.

3
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:27,780
And Pastor Ryan was the gentleman who guided the team, that sought the Lord,

4
00:00:27,780 --> 00:00:33,940
that began to articulate what it was we were facing, that God was calling us to,

5
00:00:33,940 --> 00:00:40,460
and has practiced those items and has put it together in kind of a series.

6
00:00:40,460 --> 00:00:43,880
And unfortunately, Ryan is not here.

7
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:51,180
So, rather than trying to prepare at his place, I mean, I want to hear what he has to say.

8
00:00:51,180 --> 00:00:54,040
And I'm sure you want to hear what he has to say.

9
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:58,920
Last week, we came and did one of those messages out of order.

10
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:03,060
But I think you all got the concept, we're supposed to do 20 years.

11
00:01:03,060 --> 00:01:05,660
And it's what we're called to.

12
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:08,920
It's how we're called by the Bible to live.

13
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:10,800
It's a key piece.

14
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:20,660
Rather than try to take one of those out of spec and perhaps someone else, when I was asked to preach today,

15
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:26,800
I'd like to share a message that I have been actually hoping to share in this room for over two years.

16
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:31,160
It's a message that is in my heart.

17
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:36,100
It's a message that I think the church needs to hear.

18
00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:41,620
And as I discern the movement of God's spirit in our body,

19
00:01:41,620 --> 00:01:49,880
I think it will resonate with who we are and how we behave as a body.

20
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:57,260
It's not listed in one of our core practices, but you tell me at the end if it resonates.

21
00:01:57,260 --> 00:02:04,820
I think it's clearly biblical, but I think it's something that we do functionally, we behave in.

22
00:02:04,820 --> 00:02:10,180
Full disclosure, it is a lecture that I'm turning into a sermon.

23
00:02:10,740 --> 00:02:13,880
It's a lecture from my leadership class when I taught at the seminary.

24
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:19,340
I'll try to keep it more practical and less academic.

25
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:23,260
If I fail at that, you can let me know that, too.

26
00:02:23,260 --> 00:02:24,620
But we'll try to.

27
00:02:24,620 --> 00:02:25,780
Okay.

28
00:02:25,780 --> 00:02:29,620
If you're having a chance to get that, mention that.

29
00:02:29,620 --> 00:02:32,900
I know we have some technical difficulties today,

30
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:36,340
but that'll help me know whether it'll advance or not.

31
00:02:38,180 --> 00:02:41,000
I suspect that most of you would hold the tone of servant leadership.

32
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:50,200
So, the kind of servant leadership was actually coined by Greenleaf back in an essay in 1970.

33
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:58,320
A lot of leadership thought, a lot of leadership principle has come out of Robert Greenleaf's essay.

34
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:07,440
And I think it's a very helpful term, because as I look at the life of Jesus,

35
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:11,360
I clearly see a servant leader.

36
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:20,540
I see one who came to serve, and in serving, actually lead these for us.

37
00:03:21,540 --> 00:03:28,580
I had a colleague back in seminary who tried to develop an inventory on this whole servant leadership.

38
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:31,700
And I have to be honest, he didn't get it.

39
00:03:31,700 --> 00:03:35,980
This is an inventory, but he did.

40
00:03:35,980 --> 00:03:41,340
Servant is something here, and leadership is something here, and this continuum.

41
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:49,060
And the purpose of his inventory was to find out where you fell on this continuum of servant versus leader.

42
00:03:49,060 --> 00:03:51,260
And that's missing the point.

43
00:03:51,260 --> 00:03:55,920
It's kind of like saying, you know, is Jesus human or divine?

44
00:03:55,920 --> 00:03:58,700
You know, where does he fall on the continuum?

45
00:03:58,700 --> 00:04:01,940
Well, he falls 100% on the continuum as human and divine.

46
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:11,160
And so, too, the concept of servant leadership is that we are both fervent, and we are leaders.

47
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:19,620
Greenleaf made the comment in his essay, and it's part of what really made it take off,

48
00:04:19,620 --> 00:04:26,260
that generally, high-quality leaders don't start with leadership.

49
00:04:26,260 --> 00:04:29,160
They start with ferventhood.

50
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:39,700
The individuals who know the need to serve, feel the need to serve, and begin to serve in the midst of serving,

51
00:04:39,700 --> 00:04:49,060
recognize this impetus, this falling, this bubbling up within them, this need to, in fact, lead.

52
00:04:49,060 --> 00:04:57,080
What I find that really helpful is because it's actually what Paul describes of Jesus in Philippians chapter 2.

53
00:04:57,080 --> 00:04:58,760
It's a passage that you're all familiar with.

54
00:04:58,760 --> 00:05:06,580
But watch the flow of this passage, and notice in the flow of this passage that Paul is describing Jesus,

55
00:05:06,580 --> 00:05:12,840
but in describing Jesus, he's saying, we are to be like Jesus.

56
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:21,900
So, this pattern that you see in Hebrews in Philippians 2, verses 5 through, I think it's like 11, something like that.

57
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:23,620
Yeah, 11.

58
00:05:24,340 --> 00:05:27,480
It's something that he tells us that he tells us that we're to emulate.

59
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:29,360
Here it is.

60
00:05:29,360 --> 00:05:31,880
I think I'm reading out of the NIV.

61
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:33,220
Yeah, NIV.

62
00:05:35,820 --> 00:05:43,100
In our relationship with one another, have the same mindset as Christ Jesus.

63
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:54,560
Beginning in the very nature of God, did not consider equality with God something to be used for his own advantage.

64
00:05:55,560 --> 00:06:16,680
But rather made himself nothing, or other translations say, emptied himself, by taking the very nature of a servant, and being made in human likeness, and being found in appearance as a man who humbled himself, and became obedient to death, even death on the cross.

65
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:30,940
So, Jesus, stepping into our existence here on earth, in his incarnation, and it says, from eternity into time, takes on the form of a servant.

66
00:06:30,940 --> 00:06:38,440
Then Paul goes on to say, therefore, God exalted him to the highest place.

67
00:06:39,420 --> 00:06:54,540
So, here is Jesus, who is fully God, in total union with the Father, in total union with the Spirit, in heaven, I don't know, in all life, in eternity, in everywhere, in everything, at all time, all at the same time.

68
00:06:54,540 --> 00:07:00,440
And from that, he comes and steps into our time context.

69
00:07:00,440 --> 00:07:02,620
And he says to the Spirit.

70
00:07:04,660 --> 00:07:33,340
And the Scriptures tell us, because he did that, therefore, God exalted him to the highest place, and gave him a name that is above every name, that with the name of Jesus, every name shall be, in heaven, and on earth, and under the earth, and every tongue acknowledge that Jesus Christ is Lord, and not to the glory of the Father.

71
00:07:34,660 --> 00:07:43,780
So, Jesus became the ultimate servant, and in becoming the ultimate servant, he became the ultimate leader.

72
00:07:43,780 --> 00:07:48,400
And Paul says, would you kind of act like him a little bit?

73
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:51,660
Let's tell them.

74
00:07:53,080 --> 00:07:55,440
I want to walk through that with you, if I can.

75
00:07:55,440 --> 00:08:14,040
And so, in my 40 years of leading in the church, I kind of have done through probably about a dozen short-pissing statements that have formed a bedrock of my own leadership philosophy.

76
00:08:15,240 --> 00:08:21,840
You've probably heard me mention some of them, you know, what you promote, so if you're going to leave, you've got to be careful about what you promote.

77
00:08:21,840 --> 00:08:25,520
We preach what we know, what we reproduce, what we are.

78
00:08:25,520 --> 00:08:28,260
People own what they help create.

79
00:08:28,260 --> 00:08:30,360
I mean, there's about a dozen of them.

80
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:33,320
They just form a bedrock.

81
00:08:33,700 --> 00:08:48,420
And this one in particular, that I want to talk about today, is one of those bedrock pieces for me that I think comes out of those root concepts, and then I'm going to focus on other concepts, the concepts you can't read today.

82
00:08:48,420 --> 00:08:50,360
So, here's my premise.

83
00:08:50,360 --> 00:08:54,320
Fervent leaders have responsibility.

84
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:54,980
Is that fair?

85
00:08:56,360 --> 00:09:01,260
I mean, you've got to do something in your servant leadership.

86
00:09:01,260 --> 00:09:06,060
Fervent leaders also have authority.

87
00:09:06,060 --> 00:09:18,460
Because they have the, not just the responsibility to do it, but the capacity, the right, the authority to actually do it.

88
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:21,540
And then, a third one is privilege.

89
00:09:21,540 --> 00:09:29,640
That along with authority, and along with responsibility, comes a privilege.

90
00:09:29,640 --> 00:09:38,520
And it's my premise, that when those three are read well, that we do it the way Jesus did.

91
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:41,260
And I'm going to show you that in the Scriptures.

92
00:09:41,260 --> 00:09:46,160
But much of what I want to talk about today, is when we don't do that well.

93
00:09:46,940 --> 00:09:50,940
By the way, whenever I share this with people, they often go, no, wait a second, let's just privilege stuff.

94
00:09:50,940 --> 00:09:54,800
Any of you get to fly on Air Force One?

95
00:09:54,800 --> 00:09:58,340
I mean, why not?

96
00:09:58,340 --> 00:10:01,940
You're as human as the president is, aren't you?

97
00:10:01,940 --> 00:10:04,760
I mean, we're all important, aren't we?

98
00:10:04,760 --> 00:10:07,960
We're all equally of value, aren't we?

99
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:19,840
Well, the truth is, I don't get to fly on Air Force One, because I don't have the same level of authority or responsibility that requires the privilege of having my own personal plane.

100
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:23,400
Now, when this church is 4,000, maybe we'll get one for me.

101
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:23,760
I don't know.

102
00:10:23,760 --> 00:10:29,300
But at least at this point, there is a level.

103
00:10:29,300 --> 00:10:31,880
We have people who have keys here, and people who don't.

104
00:10:34,020 --> 00:10:35,320
That's a privilege.

105
00:10:35,320 --> 00:10:38,440
Most of you probably are like, I don't want a key.

106
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:44,800
Not because you don't want the privilege, but you realize that there's an authority and responsibility that goes along with the privilege.

107
00:10:46,260 --> 00:10:54,060
So, when we're writing three together, we find a whole functional servant leader.

108
00:10:54,060 --> 00:11:02,200
And I would argue that whenever they get out of balance, we end up with a dysfunctional leader.

109
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:11,980
And let me see if I can show you that in the end of the passage that Kate read.

110
00:11:12,700 --> 00:11:15,540
Let me get there if I'll go over with you as well.

111
00:11:15,540 --> 00:11:18,400
Gospel of John.

112
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:23,060
Now, what's what Jesus is doing in this passage?

113
00:11:23,060 --> 00:11:36,040
He is telling you that in some semblance, he's inviting you into a paradigm of leadership that parallels his.

114
00:11:37,300 --> 00:11:41,600
He's inviting you into almost an earthly parity.

115
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:44,540
Now, that doesn't mean we're God.

116
00:11:44,540 --> 00:11:47,100
I know some people want to think they're right.

117
00:11:47,100 --> 00:11:55,280
But there's this invitation into this, as Jesus did, he now asks us to do.

118
00:11:55,280 --> 00:11:56,680
Watch it as he goes through.

119
00:11:56,680 --> 00:12:01,960
As the Father loved me, so I've loved you.

120
00:12:02,800 --> 00:12:07,360
But is this between what I get or what you get?

121
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:13,420
If you keep my commandments, you will remain in my love just as I was.

122
00:12:15,320 --> 00:12:16,980
You can open your Bibles if you want.

123
00:12:16,980 --> 00:12:17,540
That's okay.

124
00:12:17,540 --> 00:12:20,580
I mean, I love it when people check me.

125
00:12:20,580 --> 00:12:21,640
That's pretty good.

126
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:26,000
As the Father has kept my commandments.

127
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:26,600
Oh, I'm sorry.

128
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:33,620
If you keep my commandments, you will remain in my love just as I have kept my Father's commandments and remain in his love.

129
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:41,220
I have told you this so that my joy may be in you and that your joy may be complete.

130
00:12:41,220 --> 00:12:44,100
Again, it's what I receive and you receive.

131
00:12:44,100 --> 00:12:45,680
It's what I get and what you get.

132
00:12:45,680 --> 00:12:47,080
What I do and what you do.

133
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:48,420
My commandment is this.

134
00:12:48,420 --> 00:12:49,840
Love each other.

135
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:50,180
How?

136
00:12:50,180 --> 00:12:53,220
Thank you.

137
00:12:53,220 --> 00:12:53,560
We're good.

138
00:12:53,560 --> 00:12:54,720
People have to open the Bible.

139
00:12:54,720 --> 00:12:55,160
That's good.

140
00:12:55,160 --> 00:12:56,260
As I have loved you.

141
00:12:56,260 --> 00:13:03,380
There's this, again, this invitation to us to be like Jesus.

142
00:13:03,380 --> 00:13:06,840
I mean, isn't that really the Christian journey anyway?

143
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:11,920
All things work together for good for those who love God and are called according to his purpose.

144
00:13:11,920 --> 00:13:14,240
For those who before knew, he could ask me what?

145
00:13:14,240 --> 00:13:18,140
To be conformed into the image of his soul.

146
00:13:19,040 --> 00:13:26,780
That there is this process of transformation that God is doing in you and in me and his followers.

147
00:13:26,780 --> 00:13:32,400
And this process of transformation isn't just a personal benefit.

148
00:13:32,400 --> 00:13:36,160
But God has a purpose for this transformation.

149
00:13:36,160 --> 00:13:38,120
He has a plan for this transformation.

150
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:49,880
And as Jesus was a servant leader, Jesus is inviting us into the same kind of servant leadership paradigm.

151
00:13:49,880 --> 00:14:00,960
By the way, I would argue that unless you are an infant on your deathbed, and even there, I don't know that there's an exemption,

152
00:14:00,960 --> 00:14:04,880
or really sick, you are leading you something.

153
00:14:08,100 --> 00:14:19,360
Now, the level of authority and responsibility and privilege must line up with whatever area you're leading in.

154
00:14:19,360 --> 00:14:33,400
But what I really want to unpack today is this need, and I think, kind of a core practice for us that I think is core to who we are.

155
00:14:34,940 --> 00:14:41,780
That we read this authority, if we ask you to do something, we give you authority to do it.

156
00:14:41,780 --> 00:14:49,420
And there's usually some kind of privilege that enables you to actually do it.

157
00:14:49,420 --> 00:14:51,220
Look at the graphic practice for you.

158
00:14:52,820 --> 00:15:16,880
And you see the parallel between what Jesus did for you and his call to us, that in your leadership, you're to serve, in your service, you're to lead.

159
00:15:16,880 --> 00:15:34,220
And he said, you're no longer, and he's going to say it in a little bit, I no longer just call you service, but I'm inviting you into a parity, into a model, into a way of moving in the kingdom of God that I have models for you and I want you to model to.

160
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:38,020
Greater love has no one in the midst that one lays down one's life for one's friends.

161
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:40,460
You are my friends if you do what I command.

162
00:15:40,460 --> 00:15:44,860
And I no longer call you service, because a servant does not know his master's business.

163
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:47,340
Instead, I've called you friends.

164
00:15:47,340 --> 00:15:53,240
For everything that I learned from my father, I've made known to you.

165
00:15:53,240 --> 00:15:55,400
He's calling a thing to this paradigm.

166
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:59,560
You did not choose me, and here it is.

167
00:15:59,560 --> 00:16:05,060
But I chose you and appointed you.

168
00:16:05,060 --> 00:16:11,580
That in Jesus' calling of you, he's appointed you for something.

169
00:16:11,580 --> 00:16:16,080
There is an inherent authority in his appointment.

170
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:28,300
Whether it is the authority of being a mother and raising your child, whether it's the authority of a pastor who's preaching the word of God, there is an authority that goes with that.

171
00:16:28,300 --> 00:16:31,460
And it's something that he's inviting us into.

172
00:16:31,460 --> 00:16:34,060
There's also a responsibility.

173
00:16:34,060 --> 00:16:40,640
You did not choose me, but I chose you and appointed you so that you may bear fruit.

174
00:16:40,640 --> 00:16:43,640
And fruit that will rise.

175
00:16:44,640 --> 00:16:48,120
I don't know about you, but I'm really tired of bearing fruit that rise.

176
00:16:48,120 --> 00:16:51,440
I want fruit that remains.

177
00:16:51,440 --> 00:16:53,300
I really do.

178
00:16:53,300 --> 00:16:54,380
Lord, help me.

179
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:55,160
Introduce me.

180
00:16:55,160 --> 00:16:55,840
Teach me.

181
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:56,800
Lead me.

182
00:16:56,800 --> 00:17:12,080
And I'm convinced that part of, and we'll see this later as I go through the message, that part of the reason the fruit remains is because we take a higher level of leadership than is servant leadership.

183
00:17:14,140 --> 00:17:17,440
We don't just tell you what to do.

184
00:17:17,440 --> 00:17:22,840
But we want to empower you to not just do it, but to go beyond it.

185
00:17:22,840 --> 00:17:26,120
But servant leadership.

186
00:17:26,120 --> 00:17:42,560
You did not choose me, but I chose you and appointed you so that you may go and bear fruit, fruit that will rise, so that whatever you ask in my name, I will give it to you.

187
00:17:43,560 --> 00:17:44,360
Older, tell me.

188
00:17:44,360 --> 00:17:46,360
Older, tell me.

189
00:17:44,360 --> 00:17:44,560
Older, tell me.

190
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:47,200
I mean, could it come down bigger than that?

191
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:52,360
This is my command.

192
00:17:52,360 --> 00:17:54,440
Love, woman, and the whole.

193
00:17:55,240 --> 00:18:05,540
Okay, so for Ken, I want to now unpack this from kind of more dysfunctional perspectives.

194
00:18:05,540 --> 00:18:14,660
See where we go wrong, because I think often when you go wrong, we can identify with where we need to correct in this whole process.

195
00:18:16,660 --> 00:18:24,400
Okay, so have any of you ever met someone who just had more privilege and they had a quality or responsibility?

196
00:18:26,740 --> 00:18:28,100
Do you know what I'm talking about here?

197
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:32,780
The thing we use for this is spoiled bread.

198
00:18:32,780 --> 00:18:38,580
And some of us are actively raising one.

199
00:18:40,260 --> 00:18:43,060
And we have to be rewarded, careful.

200
00:18:43,060 --> 00:18:51,060
By the way, Proverbs says it this way: "An inheritance obtained early in life is not a blessing in the end."

201
00:18:51,060 --> 00:18:56,060
You know, my parents were very financially responsible.

202
00:18:56,060 --> 00:18:57,060
Thank you, mom.

203
00:18:57,060 --> 00:18:58,060
She's probably watching.

204
00:18:58,060 --> 00:18:59,060
Thank you.

205
00:18:59,060 --> 00:19:04,060
And we've talked about leaving us an inheritance.

206
00:19:04,060 --> 00:19:05,060
Thank you.

207
00:19:05,060 --> 00:19:16,060
But I remember early on saying to my parents, "Look, you, you, everything that you owed me, you gave me.

208
00:19:16,060 --> 00:19:18,060
You loved me and raised me responsibly.

209
00:19:18,060 --> 00:19:20,060
You don't owe me anything else."

210
00:19:20,060 --> 00:19:23,060
And you've done an amazing job.

211
00:19:23,060 --> 00:19:31,060
I mean, so you can do just about anything you want with what you have, what you've gained over your life.

212
00:19:31,060 --> 00:19:37,060
But I do remember at one point, and, because you know, I've seen personal kids sometimes have tension.

213
00:19:37,060 --> 00:19:40,060
Is that true?

214
00:19:45,060 --> 00:19:46,060
Is it as a sign or as a dad?

215
00:19:46,060 --> 00:19:47,060
That's the question.

216
00:19:47,060 --> 00:19:48,060
You don't have to answer.

217
00:19:48,060 --> 00:19:50,060
That's okay.

218
00:19:48,060 --> 00:19:49,060
It's both, yeah.

219
00:19:49,060 --> 00:19:57,060
So I remember at one point, saying to my parents, because I think they exploded something, I said, "You know, you can do anything you want.

220
00:19:57,060 --> 00:20:02,060
